==============================================================================
  Mutation tests  (assertion-strength validation)
==============================================================================

  Strategy: replace each named fact's body with `{}` (no constraint),
  then re-run Alloy. Each listed assertion should now FAIL on the
  mutated model. If it still PASSes, the assertion is vacuous and
  must be strengthened.

  - MUTATE F_AuditCompleteness  → runs/C-L1/mutated_F_AuditCompleteness.als
    rationale: Clearing the always-audit fact lets the model invent an authenticated RecordsLookup with no corresponding AuditEntry, which is exactly the FR-008/SC-001 violation the assertion is meant to catch.
    expected to FAIL: AuditCompleteness, FR_008_AlwaysAudit, FR_012_NoDeletePath
      - AuditCompleteness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_008_AlwaysAudit: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_012_NoDeletePath: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_CareTeamGated  → runs/C-L1/mutated_F_CareTeamGated.als
    rationale: Removing the care-team gate allows a Permitted RecordsLookup with no underlying active CareTeamMembership, i.e., a clinician accessing a record for a patient they are not on the care team of (FR-006, SC-010).
    expected to FAIL: OwnershipBasedAccess, FR_006_CareTeamGated
      - OwnershipBasedAccess: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_006_CareTeamGated: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_LeastPrivilege  → runs/C-L1/mutated_F_LeastPrivilege.als
    rationale: With least-privilege cleared, an AuditOfficer (who is denied RecordsLookup by the permission matrix) can produce a Permitted outcome, directly violating the per-role/per-endpoint authorisation matrix in contracts/http-api.md.
    expected to FAIL: LeastPrivilege, FR_011_AuditByIGOnly
      - LeastPrivilege: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_011_AuditByIGOnly: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_AuditAttribution  → runs/C-L1/mutated_F_AuditAttribution.als
    rationale: Removing the snapshot-correctness fact lets an AuditEntry record a clinician identity that does not match the actual caller of the operation it claims to describe -- the canonical misattribution failure under FR-009.
    expected to FAIL: AttributionCorrectness, FR_009_AuditFieldsSnapshot
      - AttributionCorrectness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_009_AuditFieldsSnapshot: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_ResponseShape  → runs/C-L1/mutated_F_ResponseShape.als
    rationale: Clearing the response-shape rules lets a Denied outcome ship a SummaryResponse on the wire, which is exactly the information-leak (denied vs. not-found distinguishable) that FR-007 / SC-003 forbid.
    expected to FAIL: NoInformationLeakage, FR_007_ByteEquivalentDenial
      - NoInformationLeakage: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_007_ByteEquivalentDenial: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AppendOnlyAudit  → runs/C-L1/mutated_F_AppendOnlyAudit.als
    rationale: Removing the at-most-one-audit-per-operation rule lets the model materialise two AuditEntry rows for the same Operation -- the structural shape of an UPDATE that has been split into an old + amended row, which FR-010 / SC-006 forbid.
    expected to FAIL: AppendOnly, FR_010_AuditImmutable
      - AppendOnly: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_010_AuditImmutable: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_AuthRequired  → runs/C-L1/mutated_F_AuthRequired.als
    rationale: With the auth-boundary fact removed, an unauthenticated operation can return a SummaryResponse -- a direct FR-001 / SC-004 violation (patient data observed without authentication).
    expected to FAIL: AuthRequiredEverywhere, FR_001_AuthRequired
      - AuthRequiredEverywhere: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_001_AuthRequired: FAIL (expected)

